<%- include('./partials/header', { title: 'Privacy Policy - StudentCalc Blog' }) %>

<main class="flex-1 max-w-3xl mx-auto py-12 px-4 w-full">

  <header class="mb-10">
    <p class="text-xs uppercase font-bold tracking-wider text-blue-600 mb-3">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold text-zinc-950 leading-tight mb-3" style="font-family: 'Google Sans Code';">
      Privacy Policy
    </h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-zinc-500">Last updated: October 21, 2026</p>
  </header>

  <div class="space-y-10 text-zinc-700 leading-relaxed">

    <section>
      <p>
        StudentCalc is an independent blog run by two students. This policy explains
        what information we collect when you use this site, how we use it, and the choices you have.
        We keep it short and plain on purpose.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-zinc-950 mb-3" style="font-family: 'Google Sans Code';">Information we collect</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
        <li><strong class="text-zinc-950">Account information.</strong> If you create an account, we store your name, email address and a hashed version of your password. We never store your password in plain text.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-zinc-950">Activity on the site.</strong> If you are logged in, we record which posts you have liked. We also keep a simple view count for each post, which is not tied to your identity.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-zinc-950">Technical data.</strong> Like most websites, our hosting provider and servers may log your IP address, browser type and the pages requested. We use this for security, abuse prevention (for example, limiting repeated login attempts) and keeping the site running.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-3">You can read the blog without creating an account or giving us any personal information.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-zinc-950 mb-3" style="font-family: 'Google Sans Code';">Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        When you log in, we set one cookie that keeps you signed in. It is an HTTP-only,
        secure session cookie that expires after a short time, and it is strictly necessary for
        the login to work. We do not currently use advertising or tracking cookies.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-zinc-950 mb-3" style="font-family: 'Google Sans Code';">How we use your information</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
        <li>To create and manage your account and let you like posts.</li>
        <li>To keep the site secure and prevent abuse.</li>
        <li>To respond if you contact us.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-3">We do not sell your personal information.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-zinc-950 mb-3" style="font-family: 'Google Sans Code';">Third-party services</h2>
      <p class="mb-3">To run the site we rely on other providers, who may receive limited technical data (such as your IP address) when your browser loads content from them:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
        <li><strong class="text-zinc-950">Hosting and database:</strong> Vercel (hosting) and MongoDB Atlas (database storage).</li>
        <li><strong class="text-zinc-950">Fonts and code libraries:</strong> Google Fonts and the jsDelivr CDN.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-zinc-950">Images:</strong> many images on the site are hosted by third parties such as Imgur.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-3">Each of these providers has its own privacy policy.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-zinc-950 mb-3" style="font-family: 'Google Sans Code';">Advertising, affiliate links and analytics</h2>
      <p>
        We may add display advertising, affiliate links or analytics in the future. If we do, those
        services may use cookies or similar technologies to measure traffic or show relevant ads.
        Before that happens, we will update this policy to name the services, explain what data they
        collect, and provide a way to opt out where required. Posts that contain affiliate links
        will say so clearly.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-zinc-950 mb-3" style="font-family: 'Google Sans Code';">Data retention and deletion</h2>
      <p>
        We keep your account information for as long as your account exists. You can ask us to
        delete your account and the data linked to it at any time by emailing us at the address below.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-zinc-950 mb-3" style="font-family: 'Google Sans Code';">Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask to see, correct or delete the personal information we hold about you. If you live
        in California or another US state with a consumer privacy law, you may have additional rights,
        including the right to know what we collect and to request deletion. We do not sell personal
        information. To make a request, email us and we will respond as soon as we reasonably can.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-zinc-950 mb-3" style="font-family: 'Google Sans Code';">Children</h2>
      <p>
        This site is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal
        information from them. If you believe a child has created an account, contact us and we will
        delete it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-zinc-950 mb-3" style="font-family: 'Google Sans Code';">Security</h2>
      <p>
        We use measures such as password hashing, secure cookies and rate limiting to protect your
        data. No website can guarantee perfect security, but we take it seriously.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-zinc-950 mb-3" style="font-family: 'Google Sans Code';">Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy from time to time. When we do, we will change the "Last updated"
        date at the top of this page.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="rounded-md bg-zinc-50 border border-zinc-200 p-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-zinc-950 mb-2" style="font-family: 'Google Sans Code';">Contact us</h2>
      <p class="mb-3">Questions or requests about your data? Email us:</p>
      <a href="mailto:[your-email@example.com]" class="font-semibold text-blue-600 hover:underline">[your-email@example.com]</a>
    </section>

  </div>
</main>

<%- include('./partials/footer') %>